Checks for entry 012 (posts/012-removing-non-directory.html).

  linkguard.py  the check: runs a command and reports whether it changed
                what the paths you name are (missing, file, directory, or a
                symbolic link and where it points)
  demo.sh       builds the toy project used in the entry, offline, and
                prints its path
  mutate.py     12 deliberate breaks of linkguard.py, each run against seven
                commands with known answers

Python 3, no packages. Tested on macOS only. Run from this directory
(mutate.py reads linkguard.py and demo.sh from here). demo.sh and
mutate.py need npm.

linkguard.py describes each path with os.lstat and os.readlink before and
after the command, and does not use the command's output or exit code to
decide anything. Before judging your command it runs five controls in a
temp directory; if they do not come out as expected it stops.

  cd "$(./demo.sh)"
  python3 /path/to/checks/012/linkguard.py node_modules -- \
      npm install --no-audit --no-fund --offline
                                                  # expect: CHANGED node_modules, exit 1
  python3 mutate.py                               # expect: 10/12 killed

Exit 0: every path is what it was. 1: a path changed and the command
exited 0. 4: a path changed and the command failed. 2: the built-in
controls did not come out as expected. 3: usage error.
